  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{5}^{125}\\frac{8}{3x{log}_{5}\u2061({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x=($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\,\\operatorname{ln}\u20615$",
  "worked_solution": "Let $u={log}_{5}\u2061({x}^{2}).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}\u20615}\\cdot 2x=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}\u20615}\\,\u27f9\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u20615}{2}\\cdot \\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $5$ | $125$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $6$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{125}\\frac{8}{3x{log}_{5}\u2061({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{8}{3}{\\int }_{5}^{125}\\frac{1}{{log}_{5}\u2061({x}^{2})}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{6}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u20615}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}\u20615}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{6}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}\u20615}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}\u2061|u|){|}_{2}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}\u20615}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}\u20616-\\operatorname{ln}\u20612) \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}\u20615}{3}\\operatorname{ln}\u20613 \\\\  & =(\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{ln}\u20613)\\operatorname{ln}\u20615\\end{aligned}\n$$",
